{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 4958062,
  "courseSlug": "remix-course",
  "courseTitle": "Remix.js - The Practical Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "34676000",
      "title": "Module Summary",
      "lectureOrder": 86,
      "videoOrder": 79,
      "sourceHash": "186eb9705d842a22f9c489f3d38d9dadf41197f5d4523d19d6500e03d28c46e7",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.13,
          "end": 5.04,
          "en": "Now, that's it for this course section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.04,
          "end": 6.3,
          "en": "In this course section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.3,
          "end": 10.62,
          "en": "we again had a look at loaders and actions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.62,
          "end": 14.73,
          "en": "We saw how we can extract data from submitted forms.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.73,
          "end": 17.97,
          "en": "We learned about different ways of submitting forms,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.97,
          "end": 20.61,
          "en": "that we can do that programmatically with",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.61,
          "end": 25.32,
          "en": "the default form element or with the Remix form element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.32,
          "end": 27.96,
          "en": "and that the latter has the advantage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.96,
          "end": 30.63,
          "en": "of keeping us in a single page application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.63,
          "end": 34.08,
          "en": "where we can get the current navigation status,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.08,
          "end": 37.023,
          "en": "and we can update the UI in a nice way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.46,
          "end": 40.35,
          "en": "We also learned that we can",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.35,
          "end": 43.41,
          "en": "submit forms programmatically in yet another way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.41,
          "end": 44.243,
          "en": "like we're doing it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.243,
          "end": 46.937,
          "en": "in the expense list item with this fetcher,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.937,
          "end": 50.37,
          "en": "which basically sends a request behind the scenes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 50.37,
          "end": 53.61,
          "en": "without expecting any navigation thereafter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.61,
          "end": 56.04,
          "en": "so that we can just send or fetch data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 56.04,
          "end": 59.01,
          "en": "behind the scenes to then update the UI ourselves",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.01,
          "end": 60.993,
          "en": "without navigating anywhere else.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 61.86,
          "end": 65.01,
          "en": "And we learned that one action can also handle",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.01,
          "end": 68.01,
          "en": "multiple form submissions by different forms.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.01,
          "end": 72.21000000000001,
          "en": "For example, by differentiating by request method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 72.21000000000001,
          "end": 74.85,
          "en": "or, as we're doing it in the auth page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 74.85,
          "end": 76.95,
          "en": "by looking at some search parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 76.95,
          "end": 81.63,
          "en": "So you can use different pieces of logic in the same action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 81.63,
          "end": 84.12,
          "en": "Of course, you could also use different pieces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 84.12,
          "end": 86.64,
          "en": "of logic in the same loader.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 86.64,
          "end": 89.01,
          "en": "There, you only have one request method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 89.01,
          "end": 90.21000000000001,
          "en": "It's always get,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 90.21000000000001,
          "end": 93.57,
          "en": "but you could still differentiate by search parents.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 93.57,
          "end": 94.40299999999999,
          "en": "But in general,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 94.40299999999999,
          "end": 96.87299999999999,
          "en": "you have a lot of flexibility, as you learned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 97.77000000000001,
          "end": 100.05,
          "en": "And you also have a lot of flexibility",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 100.05,
          "end": 102.63,
          "en": "when it comes to using loader data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 102.63,
          "end": 107.19,
          "en": "The most common scenario is to use the useLoaderData hook,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 107.19,
          "end": 109.304,
          "en": "but you can also access loader data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 109.304,
          "end": 112.35,
          "en": "by using the useMatches hook,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 112.35,
          "end": 117.09,
          "en": "as we're doing it here in the expense form component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 117.09,
          "end": 121.62,
          "en": "to extract data from some parent route component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 121.62,
          "end": 125.31,
          "en": "so that data loaded by a loader in a parent route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 125.31,
          "end": 127.59,
          "en": "can be used in some child route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 127.59,
          "end": 130.623,
          "en": "by accessing the parent route via it's ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 132.09,
          "end": 134.4,
          "en": "So lots of things you can do here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 134.4,
          "end": 136.62,
          "en": "and, if things should go wrong,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 136.62,
          "end": 139.17000000000002,
          "en": "you can, of course, add error handling.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 139.17000000000002,
          "end": 140.88,
          "en": "I mean, you should always handle it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 140.88,
          "end": 143.913,
          "en": "and always be prepared that things can go wrong.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 144.87,
          "end": 147.69,
          "en": "The error boundary handles general errors,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 147.69,
          "end": 150.963,
          "en": "and the CatchBoundary handles error responses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 151.86,
          "end": 154.47,
          "en": "You should at least add them in the root page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 154.47,
          "end": 156.96,
          "en": "so that any errors thrown anywhere",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 156.96,
          "end": 158.673,
          "en": "are at least handled here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 159.51,
          "end": 161.4,
          "en": "But you can also be more specific,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 161.4,
          "end": 165.09,
          "en": "as we, for example, are on this expense analysis page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 165.09,
          "end": 167.7,
          "en": "where we handle the error response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 167.7,
          "end": 170.82,
          "en": "that might be thrown by the expenses analysis loader,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 170.82,
          "end": 173.34300000000002,
          "en": "right next to it with this CatchBoundary.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 174.69,
          "end": 176.67000000000002,
          "en": "So plenty of new things you learned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 176.67000000000002,
          "end": 179.22,
          "en": "plenty of things to experiment with,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 179.22,
          "end": 181.2,
          "en": "and I can only encourage you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 181.2,
          "end": 184.05,
          "en": "to experiment with these things.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 184.05,
          "end": 186.06,
          "en": "But with that all out of the way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 186.06,
          "end": 189.423,
          "en": "we're now ready to dive even deeper into Remix.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
